From 956ae89fa4e8d64dc065bd139c29385499869baf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:46:01 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vulkan present: AMD FSR 1 (EASU + RCAS) instead of the
 linear blit, PS3RECOMP_VK_FSR

With PS3RECOMP_VK_FSR=1 (or rsx_vulkan_set_fsr), the window's present runs
FSR 1 as two compute passes at the size the frame takes in the window: EASU
when it grows, then RCAS sharpening (alone at the same size), copied 1:1 into
the swapchain image. PS3RECOMP_VK_FSR_SHARPNESS: RCAS stops (default 0.2).
Not with a crop (stretched frames); the linear blit then, and on any setup
failure. Shaders: vulkan/rsx_vk_fsr1.comp after AMD's FSR_Pass.glsl, with
ffx_a.h and ffx_fsr1.h unmodified in vulkan/ffx (MIT); the CPU side computes
their constants with the same headers. The colour image is now also
SAMPLED. Killzone HD, 3440x1440 window at 50% internal scale: no measurable
fps cost (129.6 vs 128.7 with the blit), sharper edges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
